24:## Overview
42:## Glossary
44:- **ChartSpec**: The canonical, library-agnostic chart description (type, data, axes, theme, interactions). All adapters consume ChartSpec.
45:- **ChartAdapter**: Interface implemented by each backend. Methods: mount(container, spec), update(spec), dispose; optional: toImage().
53:## Goals
63:## Non-goals
71:## Public API
73:### Core package (chartfn)
94:  series: Array<{ name?: string; values: number[] } | Record<string, unknown>>;
97:  /** Optional labels for series */
108:  theme?: "light" | "dark" | Record<string, unknown>;
122:  update(spec: ChartSpec): void;
157:### Validation
159:- Core MUST validate ChartSpec before calling any adapter. Validation MUST check: type is a known ChartType, data.series is a non-empty array, and any required fields per type. Invalid spec MUST return `{ ok: false, error: { code: "SPEC_INVALID", message, details: { path } } }`.
163:## Data formats / protocol
165:- **ChartSpec**: JSON-serializable. series MUST be array of objects with at least one numeric array or values field for supported types. Max series length and max data points per series MAY be capped (see Limits).
167:- **Adapter handle**: update(spec) and dispose() are synchronous. toImage() is optional and returns Promise<string> (data URL or SVG string).
169:## Semantics
171:- **render(container, spec, options?)**: Resolve container to HTMLElement (if string, document.querySelector). Select adapter by options.adapter or defaultAdapter. Validate spec; if invalid, return error envelope. Call adapter.mount(container, spec). Return handle in envelope or error.
175:- **Handle.update(spec)**: Update existing chart with new spec. Adapter MUST validate spec (or delegate to core); behavior on invalid spec is adapter-defined (e.g. no-op or throw). Core does not re-validate on update.
179:## Invariants
186:## Security
192:## Limits / caps
194:- **Max series count**: 100 (configurable or fixed; MUST be documented). Specs with series length > limit MUST fail validation with SPEC_INVALID.
195:- **Max data points per series**: 10_000 (configurable or fixed). Specs exceeding MUST fail validation with SPEC_INVALID.
199:## Observability
202:- **MUST NOT log**: Full series data in production (may contain PII). Error details MAY be logged with path/code only.
205:## Compatibility / versioning
211:## Undefined / explicitly user-deferred only
215:- Specific theme tokens beyond "light" | "dark".
217:- Real-time update frequency or throttling.

